<title>MEXICO: FORECAST-Mexico 28-day Cetes seen at 23.03 pct.</title>
<headline>FORECAST-Mexico 28-day Cetes seen at 23.03 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Interest rates on Mexico's bellwether 28-day Cetes, or T-bills, are seen rising five basis points to 23.03 percent, and rates are seen mixed at longer terms, according to a Reuters' survey of nine Cetes dealers.</p>
<p>Following is a table comparing last week's primary rates versus expectations for this week's auction and the expected change in basis points.</p>
<p>    TERM	LAST WEEK    THIS WEEK'S SURVEY   CHANGE</p>
<p>    28-DAY     22.98	    23.03		   +  5 bps</p>
<p>    91-DAY     24.43	    24.39		   -  4 bps</p>
<p>    182-DAY    24.68	    24.78		   + 10 bps</p>
<p>    1-YEAR     25.54	    25.68		   + 14 bps</p>
<p>The results will be released by Banco de Mexico at 1830 EST.</p>
<p>((--Patricia Lezama, Mexico City newsroom 525 7289559))</p>
